## Professional Translation Guidelines

- Follow the [Professional Translation Quality Guidelines](mdc:.cursor/rules/professional-translation-guidelines.md) for all translation tasks to ensure high-quality and culturally appropriate translations.

## Core Translation Principles


### 1. Accuracy and Meaning Preservation
```typescript
// ✅ DO: Preserve meaning while adapting to target language
{
  "welcome": {
    "en": "Welcome to our platform",
    "es": "Bienvenido a nuestra plataforma",
    "fr": "Bienvenue sur notre plateforme",
    "it": "Benvenuto sulla nostra piattaforma",
    "pt": "Bem-vindo à nossa plataforma",
    "de": "Willkommen auf unserer Plattform",
    "nl": "Welkom op ons platform",
    "zh": "欢迎使用我们的平台",
    "ja": "プラットフォームへようこそ"
  }
}

// ❌ DON'T: Use literal translations that lose meaning
{
  "welcome": {
    "en": "Welcome to our platform",
    "es": "Bienvenido a nuestro platform", // Incorrect
    "fr": "Bienvenue à notre platform", // Incorrect
    "it": "Benvenuto al nostro platform", // Incorrect
    "pt": "Bem-vindo ao nosso platform", // Incorrect
    "de": "Willkommen zu unser platform", // Incorrect
    "nl": "Welkom op onze platform", // Incorrect
    "zh": "欢迎来到我们的platform", // Incorrect
    "ja": "私たちのplatformへようこそ" // Incorrect
  }
}
```

### 2. Natural Language Flow
```typescript
// ✅ DO: Use natural expressions in target language
{
  "uploadSuccess": {
    "en": "Your photos have been uploaded successfully",
    "es": "Tus fotos se han subido correctamente",
    "fr": "Vos photos ont été téléchargées avec succès",
    "it": "Le tue foto sono state caricate con successo",
    "pt": "Suas fotos foram enviadas com sucesso",
    "de": "Ihre Fotos wurden erfolgreich hochgeladen",
    "nl": "Je foto's zijn succesvol geüpload",
    "zh": "您的照片已成功上传",
    "ja": "写真のアップロードが完了しました"
  }
}

// ❌ DON'T: Translate word-by-word
{
  "uploadSuccess": {
    "en": "Your photos have been uploaded successfully",
    "es": "Tus fotos han sido subidas exitosamente", // Unnatural
    "fr": "Vos photos ont été uploadées successfullment", // Unnatural
    "it": "Le tue foto sono state uploadate successamente", // Unnatural
    "pt": "Suas fotos têm sido upadas sucessamente", // Unnatural
    "de": "Deine Fotos sind erfolgreich upgeloadet geworden", // Unnatural
    "nl": "Jouw foto's zijn successvol geupload geworden", // Unnatural
    "zh": "你的照片已经被成功地上传了", // Unnatural
    "ja": "あなたの写真は成功的にアップロードされました" // Unnatural
  }
}
```

### 3. Technical Considerations

- **Variable Handling**
```typescript
// ✅ DO: Maintain variable placeholders
{
  "greeting": {
    "en": "Hello, {{name}}!",
    "es": "¡Hola, {{name}}!",
    "fr": "Bonjour, {{name}} !",
    "it": "Ciao, {{name}}!",
    "pt": "Olá, {{name}}!",
    "de": "Hallo, {{name}}!",
    "nl": "Hallo, {{name}}!",
    "zh": "你好，{{name}}！",
    "ja": "こんにちは、{{name}}さん！"
  }
}

// ❌ DON'T: Modify variable syntax
{
  "greeting": {
    "en": "Hello, {{name}}!",
    "es": "¡Hola, {nombre}!", // Wrong variable format
    "fr": "Bonjour, {nom} !", // Wrong variable format
    "it": "Ciao, {nome}!", // Wrong variable format
    "pt": "Olá, {nome}!", // Wrong variable format
    "de": "Hallo, {name}!", // Wrong variable format
    "nl": "Hallo, {naam}!", // Wrong variable format
    "zh": "你好，{名字}！", // Wrong variable format
    "ja": "こんにちは、{名前}さん！" // Wrong variable format
  }
}
```

### 4. Pluralization

- **Pluralization Rules**
  ```typescript
  // ✅ DO: Use _one and _other suffixes for pluralization
  {
    "photo_one": "{{count}} photo",
    "photo_other": "{{count}} photos",
    
    "message_one": "You have {{count}} new message",
    "message_other": "You have {{count}} new messages"
  }

  // ❌ DON'T: Use _plural suffix
  {
    "photo": "{{count}} photo",
    "photo_plural": "{{count}} photos" // Wrong format
  }
  ```

- **Component Usage**
  ```typescript
  // ✅ DO: Simply pass the count parameter
  t('photo', { count: photoCount })  // i18next will automatically select the right plural form

  // ❌ DON'T: Try to handle pluralization in the component
  t(`photo${photoCount > 1 ? '_plural' : ''}`) // Wrong approach
  ```

- **Language-Specific Plural Forms**
  - Some languages have more plural forms than just singular/plural
  - Use appropriate suffixes for each language:
    - `_zero`: zero items (in languages that have special zero form)
    - `_one`: singular form
    - `_two`: dual form (in languages that have it)
    - `_few`: few items (in languages that have it)
    - `_many`: many items (in languages that have it)
    - `_other`: fallback plural form

  ```typescript
  // Example for languages with more plural forms
  {
    "file_zero": "No files",
    "file_one": "{{count}} file",
    "file_few": "{{count}} files",  // For languages like Russian (2-4 files)
    "file_many": "{{count}} files", // For languages like Russian (5+ files)
    "file_other": "{{count}} files" // Fallback
  }
  ```

- **Namespace Organization**
```typescript
// ✅ DO: Group related translations in namespaces
// auth.json
{
  "login": { ... },
  "register": { ... }
}

// ❌ DON'T: Mix unrelated translations
// common.json
{
  "login": { ... },
  "productDetails": { ... } // Should be in product namespace
}
```

#### Language-Specific Pluralization Rules

Each language has its own pluralization rules that must be followed for natural-sounding translations:

- **English (en)**
  ```typescript
  {
    "photo_one": "{{count}} photo",
    "photo_other": "{{count}} photos"
  }
  ```

- **Spanish (es)**
  ```typescript
  {
    "photo_one": "{{count}} foto",
    "photo_other": "{{count}} fotos"
  }
  ```

- **French (fr)** - Uses the same rules as English
  ```typescript
  {
    "photo_one": "{{count}} photo",
    "photo_other": "{{count}} photos"
  }
  ```

- **Italian (it)** - Uses the same rules as English
  ```typescript
  {
    "photo_one": "{{count}} foto",
    "photo_other": "{{count}} foto"  // Note: Some nouns don't change in plural
  }
  ```

- **Portuguese (pt)** - Uses the same rules as English
  ```typescript
  {
    "photo_one": "{{count}} foto",
    "photo_other": "{{count}} fotos"
  }
  ```

- **German (de)** - Uses the same rules as English, but watch for noun capitalization
  ```typescript
  {
    "photo_one": "{{count}} Foto",
    "photo_other": "{{count}} Fotos"
  }
  ```

- **Dutch (nl)** - Uses the same rules as English
  ```typescript
  {
    "photo_one": "{{count}} foto",
    "photo_other": "{{count}} foto's"  // Note: Apostrophe in plural
  }
  ```

- **Chinese (zh)** - No plural forms, uses measure words (量词)
  ```typescript
  {
    "photo_other": "{{count}}张照片"  // 张 is the measure word for flat objects
  }
  ```

- **Japanese (ja)** - No plural forms, uses counters (助数詞)
  ```typescript
  {
    "photo_other": "{{count}}枚の写真"  // 枚 is the counter for flat objects
  }
  ```

#### Special Considerations

1. **East Asian Languages (Chinese, Japanese)**
   - Don't use `_one` suffix as these languages don't have grammatical number
   - Use appropriate measure words/counters
   - Position of the number marker varies by language
   ```typescript
   // ✅ DO: Use correct measure words
   {
     "zh": {
       "photo_other": "{{count}}张照片",  // Chinese
       "person_other": "{{count}}位客人"   // Different measure word for people
     },
     "ja": {
       "photo_other": "{{count}}枚の写真",  // Japanese
       "person_other": "{{count}}人"        // Different counter for people
     }
   }

   // ❌ DON'T: Directly translate without measure words
   {
     "zh": {
       "photo_other": "{{count}}照片"  // Incorrect: missing measure word
     }
   }
   ```

2. **Germanic Languages (German, Dutch)**
   - German requires capitalization of nouns
   - Dutch uses apostrophe for some plurals
   ```typescript
   // ✅ DO: Follow language-specific rules
   {
     "de": {
       "book_one": "{{count}} Buch",
       "book_other": "{{count}} Bücher"  // Note capitalization
     },
     "nl": {
       "photo_one": "{{count}} foto",
       "photo_other": "{{count}} foto's"  // Note apostrophe
     }
   }
   ```

3. **Romance Languages (French, Italian, Portuguese, Spanish)**
   - Watch for gender agreement with numbers
   - Some Italian nouns don't change in plural
   ```typescript
   // ✅ DO: Consider gender agreement
   {
     "fr": {
       "new_photo_one": "{{count}} nouvelle photo",
       "new_photo_other": "{{count}} nouvelles photos"
     },
     "it": {
       "photo_one": "{{count}} foto",
       "photo_other": "{{count}} foto"  // Doesn't change
     }
   }
   ```

#### Common Patterns Across Languages

1. **Zero States**
   - For languages that treat zero as plural:
   ```typescript
   {
     "message_other": "No messages"  // Used for count=0
   }
   ```
   - For languages with special zero forms:
   ```typescript
   {
     "message_zero": "No messages",
     "message_one": "{{count}} message",
     "message_other": "{{count}} messages"
   }
   ```

2. **Unit Formatting**
   ```typescript
   // ✅ DO: Use appropriate spacing for units
   {
     "en": {
       "size_one": "{{count}} MB",
       "size_other": "{{count}} MB"
     },
     "fr": {
       "size_one": "{{count}} Mo",  // Note: MB becomes Mo in French
       "size_other": "{{count}} Mo"
     }
   }
   ```

3. **Ordinal Numbers**
   ```typescript
   // ✅ DO: Use language-appropriate ordinal indicators
   {
     "en": {
       "position_one": "{{count}}st place",
       "position_two": "{{count}}nd place",
       "position_few": "{{count}}rd place",
       "position_other": "{{count}}th place"
     },
     "fr": {
       "position_one": "{{count}}ère place",
       "position_other": "{{count}}e place"
     }
   }
   ```

#### Testing Pluralization

1. **Test Numbers to Check**
   - 0 (zero state)
   - 1 (singular)
   - 2 (special case in some languages)
   - 3-10 (few cases)
   - 11+ (many/other cases)
   ```typescript
   // Test script example
   const numbers = [0, 1, 2, 3, 5, 11, 21, 100];
   numbers.forEach(n => {
     console.log(i18n.t('photo', { count: n }));
   });
   ```

2. **Language-Specific Edge Cases**
   ```typescript
   // Test special cases by language
   const testCases = {
     ja: [1, 2, 10],      // Test counter variations
     zh: [1, 2, 10],      // Test measure word usage
     de: [0, 1, 2],       // Test capitalization
     nl: [0, 1, 2]        // Test apostrophe usage
   };
   ```

### 5. Implementation Guidelines

- **Adding New Languages**
```typescript
// i18n.ts
// ✅ DO: Add new language with all required namespaces
export const resources = {
  en: {
    common: commonEn,
    payment: paymentEn,
    // ... all namespaces
  },
  es: {
    common: commonEs,
    payment: paymentEs,
    // ... all namespaces
  }
}

// ❌ DON'T: Add incomplete language support
export const resources = {
  en: { /* complete */ },
  es: {
    common: commonEs
    // Missing other namespaces
  }
}
```

- **Type Safety**
```typescript
// types/i18next.d.ts
// ✅ DO: Maintain type definitions for all namespaces
declare module 'i18next' {
  interface CustomTypeOptions {
    defaultNS: 'common';
    resources: {
      common: typeof common;
      payment: typeof payment;
      // ... all namespaces
    }
  }
}
```

### 6. Quality Assurance Checklist

Before committing translations:
- [ ] Verify all variables/placeholders are preserved
- [ ] Check for consistent terminology across namespaces
- [ ] Ensure proper cultural adaptation
- [ ] Test UI for text overflow/wrapping
- [ ] Verify all required namespaces are present
- [ ] Run type checks for i18next integration
- [ ] Verify plural forms are correctly defined
- [ ] Test with different count values

### 7. Language Switcher Implementation

- Use the `LanguageSwitcher` component for consistent language selection
- Persist language preference in user settings
- Handle fallback language gracefully
- Support RTL languages when needed

```typescript
// ✅ DO: Implement proper language switching
const handleLanguageChange = async (newValue: string) => {
  i18n.changeLanguage(newValue);
  // Persist preference if user is logged in
  if (user) {
    await updateUserLanguagePreference(newValue);
  }
};

// ❌ DON'T: Change language without persistence
const handleLanguageChange = (newValue: string) => {
  i18n.changeLanguage(newValue); // Missing persistence
};
```

